{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Replacing or recreating a rejected model can leave the corrected model unavailable for up to 24 hours."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An operator cannot clear a model's default effort through PATCH, potentially preventing its use in agent roles."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Deleting a model referenced by the file-backed policy causes the daemon to fail on restart."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An older probe can overwrite newer discovery results and cause routing to refuse an available model until a later probe."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Promoting a runtime model into configuration or removing its provider can prevent the daemon from starting until configuration or catalog state is repaired."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Slow fixture startup can make the cleanup test fail after a retry creates another pair of processes, with no demonstrated runtime effect."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An eval can invoke a model discovery says is not served, consuming an attempt and potentially recording an avoidable failure."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A queued chat request can invoke a model that discovery removed while it waited, causing an avoidable failed attempt."},{"id":"C5b","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Deleting a model still referenced by the file-backed policy prevents the daemon from restarting until the policy or catalog is repaired."},{"id":"C6b","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The reproduced behavior omits smoke checks and skip reporting for explicitly disabled providers, which reduces diagnostic detail for the active configuration."}]}